course: dictionary
lesson: 9268
title: Words that name a country
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you exactly which country, place or time is meant. «Soviet» is one of them. Here it means "of or about the Soviet Union", a large communist country that existed for most of the last century.
explain: «After the Second World War the USA and the Soviet Union became rivals in the Cold War.» The word Soviet tells you which country is meant. Check the clues: the sentence is about a rivalry between two countries, so Soviet names the second one.
explain: Watch the form of the word. «The Soviets» has a capital S and an s on the end, and it means the government or people of that country. Soviet, a soviet and the Soviets are three forms, so read the words around them to see which one you have.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put "of the Soviet Union" in place of Soviet, as in «the Soviet Union republic», and see if it still makes sense. If it does, you have the right meaning.
fact: Soviet is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «Soviet times» or «Soviet Ukraine».
fact: The Soviet Union (USSR) was a large communist country, made of Russia, Ukraine and other republics, ruled from Moscow.
fact: In the space race, the Soviets sent the first satellite, Sputnik, and the first person, Yuri Gagarin, into space.
fact: In Russian history, a soviet was a workers' council in Russia; the word means «council» in Russian.
fact: When the Soviet Union ended, Ukraine, Russia and other republics became separate countries.
exercise: «Kyiv celebrated 1,500 years in 1982; the date was chosen in Soviet times.» What does Soviet times mean? | Times when the Soviet Union existed | *Times when the Soviet Union existed, and the sun was out | Times when people wrote poems | Times when the sun was shining
exercise: «The Soviets sent the first satellite, Sputnik, into space.» Who are the Soviets? | Astronauts from the USA | *The government and people of the Soviet Union | A kind of Russian dance | A group of footballers from Moscow
exercise: «...most of Ukraine became a Soviet republic.» What kind of word is Soviet here? | A question word | *An adjective, describing the republic | A verb, an action word | A noun, the name of a person
test: What was a soviet in Russian history? | A kind of Russian food | *A workers' council in Russia | A famous space rocket | A country in Europe
test: When the Soviet Union ended, which countries became separate? | The USA and Canada | *Ukraine, Russia and other republics | Germany and France | The countries of the Cold War
exam: What does «the Soviets» mean? | A workers' council | A space rocket | *The government or people of the Soviet Union | A playground game
